  "_comment": "Authored mapping for design/bin/spec_figures_check.py. Each entry ties a figure printed in spec/target-spec.md section 2 to a column of a committed PVT record CSV. `row_match` (default `row`) is the prefix of the first cell of the one section 2 table row the figure lives in; all spec-text checks are scoped to that row. `reduce` is taken over the (optionally `where`-filtered) rows; `expected` is the printed worst case and must equal the first number in `printed[0]`; `tol` must be half a unit of its last printed digit; `at` is the binding corner and must appear (as e.g. `SS / −40 °C`) in some `printed` string. Each `printed` string must occur in the row exactly as often as it is listed, and every copy of the figure's number in the row must fall inside one of them. The checker only reports; it never edits the spec or any record.",
